            <ArticleTitle>A giant congenital aneurysm of the right coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>322-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A young woman with shortness of breath was diagnosed preoperatively as having a coronary artery aneurysm. The aneurysm originated from the right coronary artery and was extraordinarily large. The aneurysm was excised successfully under extracorporeal circulation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
